# Revision 5's refusal rule: only a refusal by the floor alone bumps, and a
# refusal by the leaf's entry stops the activation. In the purge straddle - a
# pre-purge duplicate writes the row, the purge retires the entry and deletes the
# row, then the duplicate's entry write lands above the floor - the re-created
# incarnation is refused by the duplicate's entry and stops, although its own
# row write still holds. Since #5641 a retirement raises the floor to the epoch row,
# which refuses the duplicate's straddling entry write, so in this model no entry is
# ever above a held row and this is clean: a redundancy check.
MODULE: OnlySupersededRefusedEntryRefusalStops
TARGET: OnlySupersededRefused
CLASS: Invariant
EXPECT: clean (a redundancy check: the guard is implied in the model and kept for the reason in LiveAdvanceDesign.md)
SUMMARY: an entry refusal stops the activation even while its row write still holds
PERTURBS: ClaimBump, ClaimRefuse
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
CanBump(a) == Refused(a) /\ RowHolds(a) /\ BumpEpoch <= MaxEpoch
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: only a floor-only refusal bumps.
CanBump(a) == FloorRefuses(a) /\ RowHolds(a) /\ BumpEpoch <= MaxEpoch
--- END